# [Overview]($heading.id('overview'))

| Backend | Driver | Profiles | Build option |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| SQLite | [zqlite](https://github.com/karlseguin/zqlite.zig), bundled | 3.45–3.53 | `sqlite` |
| PostgreSQL | [pg.zig](https://github.com/karlseguin/pg.zig) | 15–18 | `postgres`, `postgres_tls` |

A profile in `sqlz.ziggy` selects the grammar and type rules the checker
applies. A backend can be checked without being in a project's runtime set,
but not the other way round.

# [SQLite]($heading.id('sqlite'))

```zig
var conn = try sqlz.sqlite.open(allocator, io, "app.db", .{});
defer conn.deinit();
```

Open options cover foreign keys, journal mode, synchronous mode, the busy
timeout and open flags. `sqlz.sqlite.Pool` wraps zqlite's native pool.

# [PostgreSQL]($heading.id('postgres'))

The adapter supports pools, enum codecs and one-dimensional arrays, and
checks the server version against the configured profile at connect time.
CI runs the live conformance suite against PostgreSQL 15, 16, 17 and 18.

# [Portable queries]($heading.id('portable'))

A query lists the backends it supports. Portable queries are checked against
each listed backend's catalog; backend-specific SQL is allowed for queries
that name only that backend.

# [I/O runtimes]($heading.id('io'))

Every handle takes the application's `std.Io`. The SQLite runtime is tested
on `std.Io.Threaded` and on a zio-backed `std.Io`.
